    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0812" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Colonel J. Hart Caughey to Mr. Walter S. Robertson, at
                        Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-28">28 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>601–A. General Marshall sent following letter to Chou.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“This morning I note in Trusum No. 98,<anchor n="31a" xml:id="d422-f1"/>
                        first paragraph, that the Communist member of Team 2 is restricting the
                        movements of the U. S. members. Will you please ascertain the basis for such
                        restriction.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Chou’s reply says he has dispatched a telegram to Communist general in charge of
                    Jehol area asking about restriction of Americans. Any reply will be forwarded
                    for information.</p>
                <closer><signed>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hart Caughey</hi></signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Colonel, G. S. C.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
